description:
The Department of the Navy, NAVSUP Fleet Logistics Center Norfolk (FLCN), is conducting market research to identify capable sources to provide commercial Program Management and Support Services ( PSC: R408 ) under  NAICS   541330 . The anticipated acquisition will be a Firm Fixed-Price (FFP) small-business set aside, and will require a  SECRET security clearance .&nbsp; 

The Government intends to compete and solicit this requirement exclusively among prime contract holders under the SeaPort NxG vehicle pursuant to FAR 8.104 and FAR 16.507.&nbsp; Firms that do not currently hold an active SeaPort NxG prime contract will not be eligible to participate in the subsequent solicitation.&nbsp;  

  Submission Requirements:   

 A. Company Profile:  Company Name, Address, Point of Contact (Name, Email, Phone), CAGE Code, and Unique Entity ID (UEI) 

 B. SeaPort NxG Prime Contract Number:  Provide your active SeaPort prime contract number.&nbsp; 

 C. Socioeconomic Certification:  Confirm your business size standard as a small business under NAICS 541330, and provide all active SBA-certified socioeconomic certifications, including SBA Veteran Small Business Certification (VetCert) if applicable.&nbsp; &nbsp; 

 D. Security Classification: &nbsp;Verification of an active Secret Facility Security Clearance (FCL) issued by the Defense Counterintelligence and Security Agency (DCSA) via an informal written statement.  DO NOT  send classified proof, DD Form 254s, or any other related document. This is for market research only- a written statement that your firm holds a secret security clearance is sufficient for now. 

No additional marketing or capability information is required at this time. A formal socioeconomic set-aside determination has not yet been finalized. Once a determination is made, the final solicitation will be issued directly through the SeaPort NxG / PIEE Solicitation portal, at which time all appropriately aligned SeaPort NxG Prime Contract holders will receive an automated system notification.&nbsp;
